<title>CSPro ⇄ JavaScript Conversions: String Values</title>


A CSPro string value, created as a <logiccolor>string</logiccolor>, <logiccolor>alpha</logiccolor>, or as part of an object such as a <logiccolor>List</logiccolor>, is represented as a JavaScript <link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/String">string</link>.


When converting a JavaScript value to a CSPro string, the following conversions are supported:

<table 3 header nowrap>
    <cell>JavaScript Type</cell><cell>JavaScript Value</cell><cell>CSPro Value</cell>
    <cell><link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/String">string</link></cell><cell>&mdash;</cell><cell>string</cell>
    <cell><link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Number">number</link></cell><cell>&mdash;</cell><cell>number as a string (e.g., <logiccolor>"40"</logiccolor>)</cell>
    <cell><link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Boolean">boolean</link></cell><cell><colorinline JavaScript>true</colorinline></cell><cell><logiccolor>"1"</logiccolor></cell>
    <cell><link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Boolean">boolean</link></cell><cell><colorinline JavaScript>false</colorinline></cell><cell><logiccolor>"0"</logiccolor></cell>
    <cell><link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Null">null</link></cell><cell><colorinline JavaScript>null</colorinline></cell><cell><logiccolor>""</logiccolor></cell>
</table>

Converting an <link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Object">object</link>, including an <link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Array">array</link>, or <link "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Undefined">undefined</link> results in an exception.


<seealso javascript_value_conversions.csdoc string_JSON_representation.csdoc />
